---
// The data-deletion page (also the URL for Play Console's data deletion question).
import ProseLayout from "../layouts/ProseLayout.astro";
import { app, contactEmail } from "../config";
import { hasAccounts as A, hasAiRelease as H } from "../lib/release";
---

<ProseLayout
  title={A ? "Delete your account or data" : "Delete your data"}
  description={`How to delete what ${app.name} keeps, on your phone and on its server.`}
>
  {
    A && (
      <>
        <p>
          Your {app.name} account holds your email address (and, with Google
          sign-in, the name Google shares), and every project you saved with
          its videos, photos and other files. Deleting the account deletes all
          of it from {app.name}'s server.
        </p>
        <h2>Delete your account in the app</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            Open {app.name} and go to <strong>Settings → Account</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Tap <strong>Delete account</strong>, type DELETE and confirm.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Your account, its projects and files, your sign-in details and the
          link to your Pro purchases are deleted at once. Projects on your phone
          stay on it until you delete them or uninstall {app.name}. Deleting the
          account doesn't cancel {app.name} Pro: cancel it in Google Play.
        </p>
        <h2>Delete your account without the app</h2>
        <p>
          Email{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}?subject=Delete%20my%20${app.name}%20account`}>
            {contactEmail}
          </a>{" "}
          from the address you sign in with (or the Google account's address),
          with the subject "Delete my {app.name} account". We'll delete the
          account and everything in it within 30 days and reply when it's done.
        </p>
        <h2>Delete some data, keep the account</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>A project:</strong> delete it in {app.name}. It goes from
            your account and your phones; its files are deleted 30 days later
            if no other project uses them.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloud AI usage and template links:</strong> below.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </>
    )
  }
  <p>
    {A ? "Besides your account, " : `${app.name} has no accounts. Almost everything it stores is on your phone.`}
    {
      H
        ? ` ${app.name}'s server keeps only an anonymous ID for your phone and the cloud AI it used this month (if you've used cloud AI), your ${app.name} Pro purchase records (if you bought Pro), and templates you shared as links.`
        : ` The only thing kept on ${app.name}'s server is an anonymous ID for your phone and the cloud AI minutes it used, and only if you've used cloud AI.`
    }
  </p>

  <h2>Delete your cloud data</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Open {app.name} and go to <strong>Settings → Cloud AI</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Tap <strong>Delete my cloud data</strong>, then confirm.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    {
      H
        ? `${app.name}'s server forgets this phone's anonymous ID and the cloud AI it used, and deletes the templates you shared as links (their links stop working) and its Pro purchase records, unless another phone of yours still uses them.`
        : `${app.name}'s server forgets this phone's anonymous ID and the minutes it used.`
    }{" "}
    Nothing else is kept there, and your projects aren't affected. If you use
    cloud AI again later, the phone gets a new ID.
  </p>
  {
    H && (
      <p>
        Deleting this data doesn't cancel {app.name} Pro. Cancel it in Google
        Play (<strong>Settings → {app.name} Pro → Manage in Google Play</strong>);
        Restore purchases brings Pro back to this phone while it's paid.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>Delete what's on your phone</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>A project:</strong> delete it in {app.name}; its files go with it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Working copies:</strong>
      <strong>Settings → Clear preview cache</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Crash reports:</strong>{" "}
      <strong>Settings → Crash reports → Delete</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Everything:</strong> uninstall {app.name}. That removes everything
      it stored on your phone, except videos, GIFs, audio and photos you
      exported to your gallery.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If you can't open the app</h2>
  <p>
    The anonymous ID isn't linked to your name, email or phone number, so we
    can't find a phone's data from an email alone. It's deleted automatically
    after 13 months without use. If you need help, email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> and we'll do what we
    can.
  </p>
  <p>
    More about what {app.name} does with data:{" "}
    <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
